course: dictionary
lesson: 1664
title: Chlorine in our water
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Chlorine is a chemical element with the symbol Cl. As a gas it is yellow-green, has a strong smell, and is poisonous, so it must never be breathed in on purpose. «Salt is made of sodium and chlorine», and when they join they make a new, safe substance.
explain: Chlorine also keeps water safe to use. «Cold tap water comes from a treatment works, where it is filtered and has a little chlorine added to kill germs.» The same is done in swimming pools.
explain: The pool smell is not only chlorine. «Stinging eyes and the strong pool smell come mostly from chloramines, made when chlorine mixes with sweat and wee, so shower and use the toilet before you swim.» Goggles help too: «Swimming goggles stop the chlorine in pool water from stinging your eyes.» Never mix bleach or other cleaning products, because they can release dangerous chlorine gas.
fact: Chlorine is a yellow-green gas with a strong smell.
fact: Chlorine is poisonous, so it must be handled with care.
fact: The symbol for chlorine is Cl.
fact: Chlorine is added to swimming pools and drinking water to kill germs.
fact: Sodium and chlorine join to make table salt, which is safe to eat.
exercise: What colour is chlorine gas? | Black | Purple | Bright blue | *Yellow-green
exercise: «Cold tap water has a little chlorine added to kill germs.» Why is chlorine added? | To turn the water into a gas | *To kill germs | To make the water taste sweet | To cool the water down
exercise: Why should you shower and use the toilet before you swim? | To make the pool water warmer | *Sweat and wee mix with chlorine and can make your eyes sting | Because chlorine is a solid | Chlorine only works on dry skin
test: Which symbol stands for chlorine? | *Cl | Ch | Co | Cr
test: What must you never do with bleach? | Store it in a cup | *Mix it with other cleaning products | Put it on your hair | Use it in the pool
exam: «Sodium is a soft metal that fizzes wildly in water and chlorine is a poisonous gas, but joined together they make a new, safe substance.» What is that new substance? | Bleach | Sodium metal | Chlorine gas | *Ordinary table salt
